## DJ-01 · 2026-06-12 · CyberMesh PS-69 Conflict Boundary

**Context:** Black Aegis Private Limited (founder Sanket Nadagouda) shared the CyberMesh SIEPMU proposal for DISC 14 Problem Statement 69 (IAF) and sought advisory input or introductions.

**Decision:** No engagement of any kind. Acknowledge receipt only. No technical review, no feedback, no introduction to IAF/MoD contacts, no iDEX process advisory.

**Rationale:** PS-69 is an active open iDEX/DISC 14 defence procurement process. VV serves as CSO Southern Command. Any advisory input — however informal — from a serving officer to an active bidder in a defence procurement constitutes a conflict of interest under service conduct rules, regardless of compensation. The proposal also involves SAG-grade cryptography requirements and IAF communication infrastructure, making even informal technical commentary sensitive under OSA/service conduct frameworks.

**Constraints:** This decision forecloses all engagement with CyberMesh PS-69 until post-superannuation. It also forecloses any engagement with Black Aegis Private Limited on any iDEX or defence procurement matter until Army exit.

**Review trigger:** May 2027 (Army exit) — reassess iDEX ecosystem advisory positioning at that time. Check whether PS-69 award has been made; if CyberMesh won, assess whether residual conflict applies before any engagement.

