## DJ-02 · 2026-06-12 · CyberMesh PS-74 Conflict Boundary

**Context:** Same founder and company as DJ-01. Black Aegis Private Limited shared the CyberMesh Cyber Deception Framework proposal for DISC 14 Problem Statement 74 (IAF) alongside PS-69.

**Decision:** No engagement of any kind. Same boundary as DJ-01. The joint-company assessment means engagement with either PS-69 or PS-74 constitutes engagement with both.

**Rationale:** Identical to DJ-01, with an additional dimension: PS-74 involves active cyber deception techniques deployed against IAF network infrastructure. Serving CISO advisory input on active deception architecture for a live defence environment is particularly sensitive beyond ordinary procurement conflict.

**Constraints:** Forecloses all Black Aegis / CyberMesh engagement on any iDEX or defence matter until Army exit. The PS-74 cyber deception scope adds an additional reason to ensure post-superannuation residual conflict is assessed before any technical engagement even then.

**Review trigger:** May 2027 (Army exit) — reassess jointly with DJ-01.

