## DJ-03 · 2026-06-12 · Offline Intelligence Scope Boundary

**Context:** Akhil Pamarthy (Offline Intelligence) shared a seed-stage pitch for sovereign AI infrastructure. The pitch explicitly references DRDO and iDEX engagement in the go-to-market Phase 2.

**Decision:** Engage on commercial/legal AI angle only. Explicitly defer DRDO and iDEX conversations to post-superannuation. Any response to Akhil Pamarthy must clearly state this boundary. No introductions to DRDO contacts, no India defence market advisory, no iDEX positioning advice.

**Rationale:** The commercial sovereign AI angle (DPDP-aligned data sovereignty, legal AI compliance architecture, enterprise air-gapped deployment) carries no serving-officer conflict and is within VV's advisory positioning. The DRDO/iDEX angle creates the same conflict risk as CyberMesh — serving officer advisory input on defence market entry while in uniform is a conduct risk regardless of whether the product is dual-use.

**Constraints:** This decision forecloses DRDO introductions and iDEX advisory until Army exit. It does not foreclose: informal advisory on commercial AI governance framing, DPDP positioning, and data sovereignty (non-defence) — subject to normal service conduct norms for personal advisory activity.

**Review trigger:** May 2027 (Army exit) — reassess DRDO/iDEX advisory positioning. Before then, if Offline Intelligence requests any India defence market input, decline and log.

